  "description": "Tune27 T27-9 (\u00a710.16): `while (i < 4)` is a literal extent, the nested counter `j` declared inside the body joins the proof, and the finite fact starting at zero proves it non-negative -- so pair_sums has no contract boundary and no checked load; the literal extent base is an immediate and the reads are raw lane loads (the null arms in the generic sibling stay as double immediates, never calls). Tune27 \u00a710.15: the float null lane is a double immediate (`dmov r, nan`), never the zero-argument lambda_float_null_lane_c call. The body's checks are the raw entry's two `float[]` parameter admissions (D8.3.2: the check lives in the callee, once per crossing) and the terminal null rejections of the `dx`/`dy` float declarations in the finite loops' generic sibling arms; the dense arm has none, and no read is a checked load.",
